# Energy shield (server/README.md "Energy shield"): a per-player pool above the health that items give. Damage order:
# mana shield (utamo vita) -> the onHealthChange scripts (resistances, dodge, block, damage reductions, reflect / thorns,
# Last Breath and the other lethal-hit catches, which count health + shield) -> energy shield -> health. Not
# COMBAT_UNDEFINEDDAMAGE (scripted health costs), as the mana shield. Every hit that takes mana, shield or health (also
# damage over time and fields) restarts the recharge delay; healing never fills the shield.
#   * Player: energyShield / maxEnergyShield / energyShieldRecharge (per mille of the maximum per second, default 200 =
#     20%); Player::onThink recharges it once the delay (config energyShieldRechargeDelay, 2000 ms) has passed, only for
#     the part of the think after the delay; death empties it; a new login starts at 0 (the scripts set the maximum).
#   * Game::combatChangeHealth takes it after the HEALTHCHANGE events (in the call they re-enter with ORIGIN_NONE, so
#     once per hit), with "You lose N energy shield ..." messages and a light blue-violet number (colour 131).
#   * CombatDamage::absorbed: what the shield took. The attacker's life / mana leech counts it (single target and area),
#     so a hit on a shielded player leeches like a hit on the health.
#   * client: extended opcode energyShieldOpcode (default 224, 0 = none), plain text "es:<current>:<max>", only to
#     OTClient-based clients, at most every 200 ms (a skipped update goes out with the next think), immediately when the
#     maximum changes (client module game_energyshield).
#   * Lua: player:getEnergyShield(), player:setEnergyShield(n) (clamped), player:getMaxEnergyShield(),
#     player:setMaxEnergyShield(n) (lowers the current value), player:getEnergyShieldRecharge(),
#     player:setEnergyShieldRecharge(perMillePerSecond); configKeys.ENERGY_SHIELD_RECHARGE_DELAY / ENERGY_SHIELD_OPCODE.
#     data/lib/chaos_energy_shield.lua holds the item modifiers; data/scripts/chaos/item_mods.lua sets the maximum.
# Apply in the server source root after 0001-0014: patch -p1 < 0015-energy-shield.patch, then rebuild.
